# Triboonacci Sequence (Sum of Three Preceding Terms)

The sequence is defined as:
- `T(0) = 0`
- `T(1) = -1`
- `T(2) = -1`
- `T(n) = T(n-1) + T(n-2) + T(n-3)` for `n >= 3`

## Recursive Solution

```cpp
#include <iostream>

// Function to find the nth number in the sequence using recursion
int triboonacci(int n) {
    // Base cases
    if (n == 0) return 0;
    if (n == 1) return -1;
    if (n == 2) return -1;

    // Recursive case: sum of the three preceding numbers
    return triboonacci(n - 1) + triboonacci(n - 2) + triboonacci(n - 3);
}

int main() {
    int n;

    std::cout << "Enter the value of n: ";
    std::cin >> n;

    if (n < 0) {
        std::cout << "Please enter a non-negative integer." << std::endl;
        return 1;
    }

    std::cout << "The " << n << "th number in the sequence is: " << triboonacci(n) << std::endl;

    return 0;
}
```

